From be0c928625c7b91b7a07252291d4da2717b3ede3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 02:59:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1013/1015] wifi: mt76: mt7996: add MLO debug counters and an
 optional event log

Debugging MLO on mt7996 is hard because the firmware decides most of what
happens on air. Add a few cheap counters and an opt-in log that made the
issues on a Gemtek W1700K (AN7581 + MT7996, NPU offload) visible:

- debugfs mt76/mlo_dbg:
  - the link that tx_prepare_skb picked per TID (by the odd/even TID rule
    and after mt7996_get_tx_wcid), and how many frames were 802.3
  - the link of the wcid in each TX-free event of an MLO peer
  - per TID: calls of mt7996_tx_check_aggr, frames that are not QoS data,
    ampdu_state already set, and the result of
    ieee80211_start_tx_ba_session (last error)
  - per MLO peer link: wcid, link id, phy, link_valid, deflink/seclink,
    PEER_MLD links, MLD index, connection state, ampdu_state, BA masks
  - writing anything resets the counters
- module parameter mlo_debug (0644, default off): log PEER_MLD,
  MLD_SETUP, change_sta_links, station events and ampdu actions with
  dev_info and "mlo-dbg:" so they can be lined up with the peer.

No functional change.
